# OSC: the window title (0, 2) and the shell's working directory (7).

=== OSC 0 sets the title, ended by BEL
ref:    xterm/ctlseqs.txt OSC Ps ; Pt ST
quote:  "Ps = 0  -> Change Icon Name and Window Title to Pt."
ref:    ghostty/osc/0.mdx#Change Icon and Window Title (OSC 0)
quote:  "Since Ghostty does not support changing the window icon, this is treated as an alias of [Change Window Title (OSC 2)]."
size:   10x1
input:  "\x1b]0;hello\x07"
title:  "hello"
screen:
  |          |

=== OSC 2 sets the title, ended by ST
ref:    xterm/ctlseqs.txt OSC Ps ; Pt ST
quote:  "Ps = 2  -> Change Window Title to Pt."
ref:    xterm/ctlseqs.txt OSC Ps ; Pt ST
quote:  "XTerm accepts either BEL  or ST  for terminating OSC sequences"
size:   10x1
input:  "\x1b]2;one\x07\x1b]2;two words\x1b\\"
title:  "two words"

=== OSC 2 takes UTF-8
ref:    ghostty/osc/2.mdx#Change Window Title (OSC 2)
quote:  "Ghostty always unconditionally expects `t` to be directly UTF-8-encoded."
size:   10x1
input:  "\x1b]2;café ☕\x07"
title:  "café ☕"

=== a title split across writes
ref:    xterm/ctlseqs.txt OSC Ps ; Pt ST
quote:  "Ps = 2  -> Change Window Title to Pt."
size:   10x1
setup:  "\x1b]2;sp"
input:  "lit\x07x"
title:  "split"
screen:
  |x         |

=== OSC 7 reports the working directory as a file URL
ref:    ghostty/osc/7.mdx#Change Working Directory (OSC 7)
quote:  "Change the current working directory to the path denoted by the URI `u`. The URI should always have a scheme of `file://` and point to an existent folder."
size:   10x1
input:  "\x1b]7;file://myhost/home/me/my%20src\x07"
cwd:    /home/me/my src
screen:
  |          |
